#: POST_PROCESSING.md:1
msgid "Analyze the Results and Post-Processing"
msgstr "結果の解析と後処理"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:3
msgid ""
"Besides the diffusion of the CVs, you can perform a block analysis to assess"
" the error and check the simulation's convergence. The PLUMED [error "
"analysis](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/002/data/NAVIGATION.html) and "
"[metadynamics](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html) tutorials discuss these "
"in more detail. This section provides some guidelines on reweighing the "
"simulation to obtain the free energy surface."
msgstr ""
"CVs の Diffusion だけでなく、Block Analysis を行って誤差や収束性を評価できる。PLUMED "
"の[誤差解析](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/002/data/NAVIGATION.html)と "
"[Metadynamics](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html) "
"のチュートリアルに詳しい説明がある。このセクションでは、Reweighting によって自由エネルギー面を求めるための指針を示す。"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:5
msgid "Reweighing Multiple Walkers Metadynamics Simulations"
msgstr "Multiple Walkers Metadynamics の Reweighting"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:7
msgid ""
"You may have already been introduced to the two main routes of reweighing a "
"metadynamics simulation from the PLUMED metadynamics tutorial: [Calculate "
"the weights from the time-dependence of the metadynamics bias "
"potential](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/jp504920s) or [calculate the "
"weights from the metadynamics bias potential obtained at the end of the "
"simulation](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/ct3002464). This tutorial "
"uses the former way as an example."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED の Metadynamics チュートリアルでは、Reweighting "
"の主な2つの方法をすでに学んだかもしれない。[Metadynamics の BiasPotential の時間依存性から Weight "
"を計算する方法](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/jp504920s)と、[シミュレーション終了時の "
"BiasPotential から Weight "
"を計算する方法](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/ct3002464)である。ここでは前者を例に使う。"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:9
msgid ""
"To reweigh the frames from multiple walkers metadynamics simulations, you "
"can perform the reweighing for each walker independently and then combine "
"all the histograms to convert the free energy surface. You can construct a "
"`plumed_reweight.dat` file for each walker as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Multiple Walkers Metadynamics の Frames を Reweighting するには、各 Walker "
"を独立に処理してから、すべての Histograms を統合して自由エネルギー面へ変換すればよい。各 Walker 用の "
"`plumed_reweight.dat` は、次のように作成できる。"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:25
msgid ""
"Note that you will need to determine the values of CLEAR in HISTOGRAM and "
"STRIDE in DUMPGRID for the block size in your block analysis. You can "
"perform the reweighing using PLUMED tools:"
msgstr ""
"Block Analysis の Block Size に応じて、HISTOGRAM の CLEAR と DUMPGRID の STRIDE "
"の値を決める必要がある。Reweighting は PLUMED のツールで実行できる。"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:30
msgid ""
"After reweighing all the walkers, you can combine all the histograms to "
"calculate the free energy and the associated error. You can either do it "
"using PLUMED or with the following Python script:"
msgstr ""
"すべての Walkers を Reweighting したら、Histograms "
"を統合し、自由エネルギーとその誤差を計算できる。PLUMED、または次の Python スクリプトを使う。"

#: POST_PROCESSING.md:80
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you may want to reweigh the simulation on a different CV, which "
"is not biased through the metadynamics simulation. In this case, you just "
"need to modify the `plumed_reweight.dat` file to inform PLUMED tools to read"
" a different CV column from the COLVAR file:"
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics で Bias を加えていない別の CV について Reweighting したい場合もある。その場合は、COLVAR の別の "
"CV 列を読むように、`plumed_reweight.dat` を変更するだけでよい。"
